WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.980
Comparative passages are not harder. I have good news.

2
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.860
This is good news, but I feel like because I'm myth-busting it feels like bad news

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.700
even though it's good news, but it is good news.

4
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.280
You don't have to really do that much specialized

5
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.400
anything on comparative passages.

6
00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:19.040
Sure, we'll have a few quick tips, but I don't want you to take from these few

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.900
quick tips that you need to be afraid of comparative passages, or you

8
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.050
always need to do them last because they take longer, or anything like that,

9
00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.720
because that's really not true. Very often, students will do exactly the same on

10
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.580
comparative passages in aggregate or sometimes even a little bit better.

11
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:38.129
Often the challenges when you see scores going down in comparative passages, it's

12
00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.000
because people have so many meta techniques and anxieties that they're applying to

13
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:45.980
this special area of comparatives that it drowns

14
00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.800
out just what should be the star, which is the content of the passage.

15
00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.220
And so I don't want you to overthink these.

16
00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.800
The more you meta think about it, the worse it's going to be.

17
00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.520
And so just a few simple things. Don't pre-assume that the

18
00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.540
passages are going to relate to each other in any sort of predefined way.

19
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:04.340
Sometimes I'll have students that they'll be like, "I was so upset

20
00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.540
because there isn't a disagreement here.

21
00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.220
I don't see what they disagree on at all." And it's like, yeah, that's because they

22
00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.090
don't disagree on anything. Why did you come in assuming that

23
00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.900
these two were going to disagree? Comparative passages are not debates on logical

24
00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.960
reasoning. They're just two articles that are going to have some kind of

25
00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.680
relationship, but they could have a million different kinds of relationships.

26
00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.240
There could be

27
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.380
a short statute and an implementation of the statute.

28
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:30.400
There could be

29
00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.460
rumination on the same topic, but in different domains, let's say.

30
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.870
Maybe domains of law, maybe domains of music. Who even knows?

31
00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:41.340
And so you don't want to come in with that preset agenda.

32
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:44.660
You just want to let the passage take the lead, and the passages are going to tell

33
00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:47.480
you how they relate to each other. It's not that big of a deal.

34
00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:51.240
These are just two excerpted pieces of writing from real texts

35
00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:55.420
that the people who make the LSAT thought had some kind of reason to be next to

36
00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.350
each other. And so don't overthink it and make it harder than it has

37
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.320
to be. So we're going to talk about a few ways to not overcomplicate comparative

38
00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.260
decks in terms of your process, and then also some specialist tips and tricks on

39
00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:09.801
comparative translation that I'm really excited to get into.

40
00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:13.090
And so I cannot wait to hear your feedback, and you guys can tell me all why I'm

41
00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.030
wrong and comparatives actually are harder, but

42
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.640
they really aren't. It's fine.

